From 37cbdb8cec661522dd995630ca1590463261eae0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sohnyj <271139641+sohnyj@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:54:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter: add cropdetect_cuda filter

CUDA port of the black mode of cropdetect, for frames decoded with
nvdec. A kernel sums up the luma plane per row and per column, and the
borders are then searched on the CPU with the logic of vf_cropdetect.c,
so that the metadata and the log output match those of the software
filter.

Each block stores its tile of samples in shared memory and sums up its
rows and columns from there. compat/cuda/cuda_runtime.h now defines
__shared__ for clang, as no kernel used shared memory so far.

The samples are read through the pitch of the frame and shifted down to
their code values, so the rows that a decoder allocates below the frame
are not read, and the sums are copied to page-locked host memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
